#
# NVIDIA Knowledge Foundation configuration.
#   ./scripts/demo.sh init            creates .env from this file (mode 600) and generates section 5
#   ./scripts/demo.sh doctor --keys   checks it, including that every model id is listed by its endpoint
#
# Keep comments on their own lines, never after a value. Never commit .env.
# `./scripts/demo.sh replay` needs none of this file.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Inference endpoint: the agent's models, and Auto Ontology's
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The keys are read only by Switchyard, the model router outside the sandbox, by Auto Ontology
# under the ontology profile, and by ingest and retrieval when RETRIEVER_API_KEY is empty. No
# model key ever enters the OpenShell sandbox.
#
# Hermes always asks for the route "knowledge"; SWITCHYARD_ROUTES picks the template
# in infra/switchyard/routes/:
#   passthrough.nemotron         every turn goes to the efficient model; no judge
#   escalation.nemotron-gpt      the efficient model answers; a GPT judge can hand the session
#                                to a capable GPT model
#   escalation.nemotron-claude   the same with Claude models (Anthropic Messages API)
#   escalation.nemotron          the same with Nemotron models only (a Nemotron judge)
#   pinned-capable.nemotron-gpt  every turn goes to the capable GPT model; no judge
#   pinned-capable.nemotron-claude  every turn goes to the capable Claude model; no judge
# In every template a Nemotron aux model (AGENT_AUX_MODEL, thinking off) serves Hermes' auxiliary
# calls and the overload fallback. The efficient, capable and judge models a template uses must all
# differ, and the aux model must differ from the efficient one.
# After editing this section run ./scripts/demo.sh restart switchyard. It keeps the sandbox.
#
# Default: build.nvidia.com, with Nemotron 3 Ultra answering every turn and Nemotron 3 Super
# serving the auxiliary calls.
INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# An nvapi- key from build.nvidia.com. It also serves section 2 unless RETRIEVER_API_KEY is set.
INFERENCE_API_KEY=
SWITCHYARD_ROUTES=passthrough.nemotron
AGENT_EFFICIENT_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b
AGENT_AUX_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
SWITCHYARD_CONFIRMATIONS=1
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_REASONING_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_NON_REASONING_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint that serves every model instead (for example an internal gateway): set
# INFERENCE_BASE_URL and INFERENCE_API_KEY to it and use the model ids it lists. doctor --keys checks that
# every id the template uses is listed. For instance:
# INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://<gateway>/v1
# AGENT_EFFICIENT_MODEL=nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra
# AGENT_AUX_MODEL=nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3-super-v3
#
# A frontier model from a provider serving it (the *-gpt and *-claude templates; build.nvidia.com
# serves none). An empty CAPABLE_BASE_URL means INFERENCE_BASE_URL, and an empty CAPABLE_API_KEY means
# INFERENCE_API_KEY only on that same endpoint: the inference key never goes to another host.
# SWITCHYARD_ROUTES=escalation.nemotron-gpt
# AGENT_CAPABLE_MODEL=<the frontier model's id at that provider>
# AGENT_JUDGE_MODEL=<the judge's id at that provider>
# CAPABLE_BASE_URL=https://<a provider serving the frontier model>/v1
# CAPABLE_API_KEY=<that provider's key>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Retriever endpoint: document embedding (ingest, retrieval) and reranking (retrieval)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
RETRIEVER_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# Empty: INFERENCE_API_KEY. Set it when section 1 uses a key that is not an nvapi- key.
RETRIEVER_API_KEY=
RETRIEVER_EMBED_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b
# Empty: no reranking (hits keep their vector order). Set it empty for a gateway without NVIDIA's /ranking API.
RETRIEVER_RERANK_MODEL=nvidia/llama-nemotron-rerank-vl-1b-v2
# Empty: the reranker's hosted build.nvidia.com endpoint. Otherwise a full rerank URL,
# e.g. a self-hosted NIM's http://<host>:8000/v1/ranking.
RETRIEVER_RERANK_URL=
# Changing the embed model needs a rebuild of the index: ./scripts/demo.sh down --volumes, then up (packs re-ingest).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. What runs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# core is always on: UI, API, ingest, Milvus, the retrieval and tables tools, Switchyard, Phoenix and the
# Hermes agent in its OpenShell sandbox. Add any of:
#   parse        NVIDIA Nemotron Parse 2.0 on vLLM (an NVIDIA GPU): parses PDFs, scans and images
#   kumo         Kumo Relational NIM and the prediction tool (x86_64 and an NVIDIA GPU)
#   prediction   the prediction tool alone, against a remote Kumo Relational NIM (KUMO_RELATIONAL_URL and
#                KUMO_API_KEY, below)
#   ontology     Auto Ontology; needs the vendor/auto-ontology submodule (repository access until it is public)
# DGX Spark: core,parse,prediction (the Kumo NIM is x86_64 only, so predictions go to a remote one).
# Brev or any x86_64 GPU host: core,parse,kumo (the NIM runs locally).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=core,parse,prediction
#
# Predictions: the remote Kumo Relational NIM. Required with the prediction profile (the default): doctor
# reports a problem while either is empty, and doctor --keys asks KUMO_RELATIONAL_URL/v1/health/ready with
# the key. Ignored under the kumo profile, which runs its own NIM (demo.sh passes it no key).
# The NIM's base URL (the one that serves /v1/health/ready). The key travels in a header, so use https: the
# Kumo client refuses to send it over plain http to anything but a local address.
KUMO_RELATIONAL_URL=
# The key of the authenticating gateway in front of that NIM, sent as the X-API-Key header.
KUMO_API_KEY=
# Every port but the UI's (UI_BIND_HOST, below) is published on 127.0.0.1 only. On a remote host,
# use an SSH tunnel.
UI_PORT=3300
# The host address the UI is published on. Keep 127.0.0.1 unless a link that requires sign-in,
# such as a Brev link with sign-in set in the Brev console, must reach the UI; then 0.0.0.0
# exposes the UI (and, through its /api/v1 proxy, the agent and uploads) to that network with no sign-in of
# its own. The API, tools, Switchyard and Phoenix stay on 127.0.0.1 whatever this says.
UI_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# The industry the UI opens on (a directory of data/packs).
DEFAULT_PACK=retail

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Ingestion
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nemotron Parse. Under the parse profile demo.sh points ingest at the local server and these stay unused.
# Without it: a hosted endpoint, e.g. https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 with PARSE_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-parse-2.0
# and an nvapi- PARSE_API_KEY; empty: PDFs are read from their text layer and images are refused.
PARSE_BASE_URL=
PARSE_API_KEY=
# PARSE_MODEL=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Parse-2.0
# The vLLM server's share of GPU memory (the DGX Spark's memory is unified: keep it small).
# PARSE_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.15
# Upload limits: per file, files per request, and the request body.
# INGEST_MAX_FILE_MB=100
# INGEST_MAX_FILES=20
# INGEST_MAX_REQUEST_MB=512
# INGEST_WORKERS=2
# Seconds one pipeline stage of one file may take (Parse may use three quarters of it).
# INGEST_STAGE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Internal secrets, generated by ./scripts/demo.sh init
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API's bearer key for Hermes' Runs API inside the sandbox (at least 16 characters).
# Changing it recreates the sandbox on the next `up`.
HERMES_API_SERVER_KEY=
# The key on the sandbox's receipt callbacks to the API. Hermes only ever sees an OpenShell
# placeholder. Changing it recreates the sandbox on the next `up`.
HERMES_RECEIPT_API_KEY=
# Auto Ontology's local admin password and session secret (ontology profile).
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_AUTH_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Optional
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto Ontology answers questions over one structured source (ontology profile).
# AUTO_ONTOLOGY_SOURCE=retail.sales
#
# Voice input: a microphone in the composer. The API sends the recording to NVIDIA Nemotron
# ASR on build.nvidia.com (nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b) and returns only its transcript.
# SPEECH_API_KEY is an nvapi- key; empty uses RETRIEVER_API_KEY when RETRIEVER_BASE_URL is
# build.nvidia.com.
# SPEECH_INPUT_ENABLED=true
# SPEECH_API_KEY=
# SPEECH_CLEANUP_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
# SPEECH_INPUT_MAX_SECONDS=60
#
# How long finished jobs stay available, in seconds.
# JOB_RETENTION_SECONDS=86400
